# Go build/test artifacts
/bin/
*.out
*.test
coverage.txt

# Go's fuzzing cache lives in GOCACHE, not here: testdata/fuzz holds the seed
# corpus, including crashers a fuzz run writes out, and those must be
# committable so a reproducer is never silently discarded.

# Per-target fuzz output, kept by `make fuzz` so a failure's message text
# survives a scrolled or piped run. It is diagnosis, not a finding: a real
# finding is the reproducer Go writes under testdata/fuzz, which is committable.
/.fuzzlogs/

# Editor/OS cruft
.DS_Store
